},{"name":"youvalv","email":"youval.vaknin@gmail.com"},{"name":"serhalp-netlify","email":"philippe.serhal@netlify.com"},{"name":"mlgualtieri-gatsby","email":"mike.gualtieri@netlify.com"}],"_nodeVersion":"24.22.1","_hasShrinkwrap":false,"_npmOperationalInternal":{"host":"s3://npm-registry-packages-npm-production","tmp":"tmp/redirect-matcher_0.8.0_1793692651721_0.487489720623812"}}},"time":{"created":"2026-10-02T11:09:31.220Z","modified":"2026-11-03T07:57:32.039Z","0.4.0":"2026-10-02T11:09:31.681Z","0.4.1":"2026-10-02T11:48:17.310Z","0.4.2":"2026-10-02T12:15:17.169Z","0.6.0":"2026-10-27T11:16:46.327Z","0.7.0":"2026-10-28T17:27:50.663Z","0.8.0":"2026-11-03T07:57:31.881Z"},"author":{"name":"Netlify Inc."},"license":"UNLICENSED","description":"Netlify's redirect rule matcher, compiled to WebAssembly","maintainers":[{"name":"netlify-bot","email":"bot@netlify.com"},{"name":"mikewen","email":"mike.wen@netlify.com"},{"name":"youvalv","email":"youval.vaknin@gmail.com"},{"name":"serhalp-netlify","email":"philippe.serhal@netlify.com"},{"name":"mlgualtieri-gatsby","email":"mike.gualtieri@netlify.com"}],"readme":"# @netlify/redirect-matcher\n\nNetlify's redirect rule matcher, compiled to WebAssembly, for matching requests\nagainst Netlify redirect rules in local tooling.\n\n```js\nimport { createMatcher } from '@netlify/redirect-matcher'\n\nconst matcher = await createMatcher(rules, { jwtSecret, jwtRoleClaim })\nconst result = matcher.match({ scheme: 'https', host, path, query, headers, cookies })\n\nif (result?.type === 'match') {\n  console.log(result.status, result.to)\n}\n\nmatcher.close()\n```\n\n`rules` is the JSON produced by `@netlify/redirect-parser`, as a string or an\narray. Rules that fail to parse are skipped and listed in\n`matcher.parseErrors`. `match` returns `null` when nothing matched, and\n`{ type: 'forcedNotFound' }` when a role-gated rule rejected the request and no\nlater rule matched.\n\n`headers` and `cookies` may be plain objects or iterables of `[name, value]`\npairs, such as `Headers` or `Map`. Header names are matched case-insensitively,\nso names that differ only in case collide, and the last one wins. A header\nwhose value is an array matches on its first element, and `null` or\n`undefined` values are treated as absent.\n\nLoading the matcher defines these globals, which Go's WebAssembly runtime\nneeds: `globalThis.Go`, `globalThis.__netlifyRedirectMatcher`, and, if they\nare not already defined, stub `globalThis.fs` and `globalThis.path` objects.\n\nRequires Node.js 22.12 or later.\n","readmeFilename":"README.md"}